WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.503
The company that
brought you Google Glass,

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:04.462
the Google self-driving car,

00:00:04.462 --> 00:00:08.842 position:56%
some of the craziest science fiction
things that you can possibly imagine

00:00:08.842 --> 00:00:11.136
is focused on
counting strawberries.

00:00:11.136 --> 00:00:12.095
And here's why.

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:18.977
For the last decade or so,

00:00:18.977 --> 00:00:22.564
Google X has been designed
to sort of go for these

00:00:22.564 --> 00:00:24.274
so-called moonshot projects.

00:00:25.483 --> 00:00:27.944
Many of these things
have not panned out.

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:32.699 position:56%
But there have been a few successes.

00:00:33.324 --> 00:00:34.993
What's happened over the years

00:00:34.993 --> 00:00:39.622
is that Google X has gone
to being much more pedestrian,

00:00:39.622 --> 00:00:41.708
but also real businesses.

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:44.627
And I think that's where
Project Mineral comes in.

00:00:46.629 --> 00:00:49.007
Mineral is working on a project

00:00:49.007 --> 00:00:51.051
to basically bring robotics

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:52.844
and machine learning
and computer vision,

00:00:52.844 --> 00:00:54.888
but to the world of agriculture.

00:00:56.097 --> 00:00:58.266
They're building
these things called rovers,

00:00:58.266 --> 00:01:02.645
which are semi-autonomous,
remote-controlled robots.

00:01:04.105 --> 00:01:07.275
When it drives over these crop
rows, it's taking pictures.

00:01:07.275 --> 00:01:08.526
And those pictures are then

00:01:08.526 --> 00:01:10.862
being fed into these
very sophisticated

00:01:10.862 --> 00:01:12.280
machine learning algorithms.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:14.407
How many strawberries
does this plant have?

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:15.366
How many leaves does it have?

00:01:15.366 --> 00:01:16.409
How tall is it?

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:17.994
What species is it?

00:01:17.994 --> 00:01:22.582
And it's trying to use that
data to help farmers say,

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:26.044 position:58%
with some certainty, which plants
are doing well and which ones aren't.

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:31.633 position:59%
So the end goal here,
it's one, is to create a business that

00:01:31.633 --> 00:01:36.221 position:59%
that generates revenue where
they are able to sell machine learning

00:01:36.221 --> 00:01:40.433 position:63%
and the robotics expertise
that they have to agriculture companies.

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:43.686
Beyond that, I think the goal
is to do farming better

00:01:43.686 --> 00:01:47.107
and in particular to help
farmers do more with less.

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:49.651
And when you talk to people at X,

00:01:49.651 --> 00:01:51.152
what they say is

00:01:51.152 --> 00:01:54.030
climate change is increasingly
a huge part of their work.

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:56.741
And you can see the
possible impact here.

00:01:56.741 --> 00:02:00.787
If farmers are able to
develop better plants that can deal

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:03.581
with rising temperatures,
if they're able to use less water,

00:02:03.581 --> 00:02:06.501
less fertilizer,
that could have a significant

00:02:06.501 --> 00:02:08.419
climate impact and it could

00:02:08.419 --> 00:02:10.255
allow us to live better lives.

